a"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Blockchain"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential applications include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Property records"},{"text":"Digital ownership records"},{"text":"Transaction verification"},{"text":"Smart contracts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PropTech"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand how technology is changing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Property transactions"},{"text":"Digital leasing"},{"text":"Property management"},{"text":"Real estate investment"},{"text":"Property analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Automated Contract Management"},{"type":"p","text":"Modern legal teams increasingly use:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Contract Creation","Review","Approval","Digital Signature","Contract Repository","Obligation Tracking","Renewal / Expiry Alerts"]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile at Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to demonstrate:"},{"type":"h","text":"Legal Knowledge"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Property law"},{"text":"Contract law"},{"text":"Land laws"},{"text":"Real estate regulation"},{"text":"Civil procedure"},{"text":"Construction law"},{"text":"Infrastructure law basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Title review"},{"text":"Property due diligence"},{"text":"Legal research"},{"text":"Contract drafting"},{"text":"Contract review"},{"text":"Risk identification"},{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Regulatory research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Ideally:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"2 property due-diligence projects"},{"text":"2 contract-drafting projects"},{"text":"1 RERA case study"},{"text":"1 JDA analysis"},{"text":"1 real estate transaction simulation"},{"text":"2+ relevant internships"},{"text":"Legal research/writing samples"}]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"REAL ESTATE LAWYER"},{"type":"p","text":"│"},{"type":"p","text":"┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐"},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"PROPERTY LAW CONTRACT LAW LAND LAW"},{"type":"p","text":"│ │ │"},{"type":"flow","items":["└─────────────────┼─────────────────┘","TITLE DUE DILIGENCE","TRANSACTION LAW","REAL ESTATE REGULATIONS","DOCUMENTATION & DRAFTING","NEGOTIATION SKILLS","┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐"]},{"type":"p","text":"↓ ↓ ↓"},{"type":"p","text":"CONSTRUCTION INFRASTRUCTURE REAL ESTATE"},{"type":"p","text":"LAW LAW FINANCE"},{"type":"p","text":"│ │ │"},{"type":"flow","items":["└─────────────────┼─────────────────┘","LEGAL TECHNOLOGY","AI + PROPTECH","REAL ESTATE LAWYER"]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Law Student","Real Estate Legal Intern","Legal Trainee / Junior Associate","Real Estate Lawyer / Associate","Senior Associate","Managing Associate","Partner / Legal Head"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative corporate pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Graduate","Legal Executive","Real Estate Legal Associate","Senior Legal Counsel","Legal Manager","Head – Legal / General Counsel"]},{"type":"h","text":"Independent pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Law Degree","Professional Qualification / Enrolment","Property Law Practice","Real Estate Litigation & Transactions","Independent Real Estate Lawyer","Real Estate Legal Consultancy"]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest profile for this career is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Integrated Law Degree","Property & Land Law","Real Estate Internship","Title Due Diligence","Contract Drafting","RERA/Regulatory Knowledge","Real Estate Transactions","Infrastructure/Construction Exposure","Real Estate Lawyer"]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Formula"},{"type":"flow","items":["Property Law","Land Law","Contract Drafting","Title Due Diligence","Real Estate Regulation","Negotiation","Transaction Management","Legal Technology = Strong Real Estate Lawyer Profile"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The key differentiator is practical transaction capability. A student who can independently understand a property's title chain, identify legal risks, review approvals, draft/review transaction documents and communicate those risks clearly to a client will be significantly better positioned than a graduate who has only studied property law theoretically."}]}]}